1
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,940
Previously on Friends:

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,160
Erica, are you okay?

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:06,900
Yeah, you know, maybe I ate too much.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:11,100
I keep getting these stomachaches. They come and go, like, every few minutes.

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:16,700
-Oh, my God. -Relax, we'll just get her some antacids.

6
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,780
She doesn't have a stomachache! She's in labor!

7
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:21,880
Oh, my God!

8
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,540
If you think that I didn't say goodbye because you don't mean as much to me as everybody else, you're wrong.

9
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,540
It's because you mean more to me.

10
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,260
-Rach! -What?

11
00:00:55,509 --> 00:00:56,319
Hey.

12
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,760
Go back to sleep. I have to go home.

13
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,100
Oh, God. This was amazing.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,740
It really was.

15
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,040
You've learned some new moves.

16
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:15,960
Yeah, well, this guy at work gave me <i>Sex for Dummies</i> as a joke.

17
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,240
- Who's laughing now? - I am.

18
00:01:20,155 --> 00:01:22,325
《老友记》第十季第十七  十八集  说再见

19
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:10,080
Breathe...

20
00:02:14,993 --> 00:02:16,723
Okay. Good.

21
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,880
Next time, can I say "breathe"?

22
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,840
No. Last time, you said it like Dracula, and it scared her.

23
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:25,280
Can I get you anything? You want some more ice chips?

24
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:26,340
No, I'm okay.

25
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,580
All right. I'll be right back.

26
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:33,260
- Where you going? - To use the bathroom.

27
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:36,640
- You can't leave me alone with her. - What?

28
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:41,600
This is exactly the kind of social situation that I am not comfortable with.

29
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:45,900
What kind of social situation are you comfortable with?

30
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:50,520
It's just that we've never spent any time, you know, alone together.

31
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:51,880
You'll be fine.

32
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,740
You won't, but I'll be back in two minutes.

33
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,140
Okay.

34
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,640
So any plans for the summer?

35
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,660
I don't know. Maybe church camp.

36
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:18,180
May not want to mention this.

37
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,280
So you ever wonder which is worse?

38
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,280
You know, going through labor or getting kicked in the nuts?

39
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,060
- What? - Oh, it's just interesting.

40
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:37,160
Because no one will ever know because no one can experience both.

41
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:44,140
One of life's great unanswerable questions.

42
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:50,380
Who knows? Maybe there's something even more painful than those things.

43
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,120
Like this.

44
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:03,900
- Come in. - Morning.

45
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,900
- Hey. - What's that?

46
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,480
Oh, it's my housewarming present for Monica and Chandler.

47
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:12,600
That's a baby chick and duck.

48
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:15,300
And I named them Chick Jr. And Duck Jr.

49
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,860
I did not see that coming.

50
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,800
They'll love it at that new house.

51
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:22,060
It has that big backyard.

52
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:26,700
When they're old, they'll go to that farm that Chandler took the other chick and duck to.

53
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:29,640
- Yes. - Yeah.

54
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:32,340
It's a shame people can't visit there.

55
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,820
That is the rule though.

56
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:40,660
Guess what. You're almost an uncle.

57
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:41,620
What?

58
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,260
Erica went into labor last night.

59
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,900
Monica and Chandler are at the hospital right now.

60
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:48,000
- Oh, my God! - I have a feeling it's gonna be a girl.

61
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:50,580
Phoebe, you were sure Ben was gonna be a girl.

62
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,120
Have you seen him throw a ball?

63
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:58,720
- Is Rachel here? - I think she's still asleep.

64
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:01,060
How did it go with you guys last night?

65
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,500
She seemed pretty pissed at you.

66
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,820
We worked things out.

67
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,060
What's that smile?

68
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,440
Did something happen with you two?

69
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,860
Hey, I'm not one to kiss and tell.

70
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,900
But I'm also not one to have sex and shut up.

71
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:16,900
We totally did it.

72
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,320
Oh, my God. You and Rachel?

73
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,000
I know, it's pretty great.

74
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,480
So, what does that mean?

75
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:24,800
Are you guys getting back together?

76
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,240
Oh, I don't know.

77
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,240
We didn't really get to talk.

78
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:29,720
But do you want to get back together?

79
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:30,940
I don't know.

80
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,920
It was incredible.

81
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:36,100
I mean, it just felt so right.

82
00:05:36,260 --> 00:05:37,180
When I was holding her,

83
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,020
I mean, I never wanted to let her go.

84
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:44,280
Know what? Yeah, I do. I want to be together.

85
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,060
So is she still going to Paris?

86
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:53,380
Wow, I hadn't thought of that. I hope not.

87
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:56,220
This is, like, the best day ever. Ever.

88
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,060
You guys might get back together.

89
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,860
Monica and Chandler get their baby.

90
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:02,040
There are chicks and ducks in the world again.

91
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,380
I feel like I'm in a musical.

92
00:06:13,012 --> 00:06:13,960
Morning.

93
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:14,920
Guess you'll never know how it ends.

94
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,180
- Hey. - Hi.

95
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:21,920
- Hi. How'd you sleep? - Good. You?

96
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,860
- Good. - I'll bet you did.

97
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,380
Would you guys mind giving us a minute?

98
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,840
Sure. Just keep an eye on the chick and duck.

99
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:34,180
Chick and the duck? Didn't they die--?

100
00:06:34,333 --> 00:06:40,353
Dive. Yeah, they dove. Headfirst into fun on the farm.

101
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:48,260
So....

102
00:06:51,451 --> 00:06:54,781
- Morning. - You too.

103
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:56,560
Last night was just wonderful.

104
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:57,860
Oh, it really was.

105
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:01,240
I woke up today with a big smile in my face.

106
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:03,300
I know, me too. It was....

107
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:07,760
You know, it was one of those things you think is never going to happen.

108
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:11,000
And then it does, and it's everything you want it to be.

109
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:14,270
I know. It was just....

110
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,240
It's just the perfect way to say goodbye.

111
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,620
Just a little bit more, honey.

112
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:30,040
Oh, man, this hurts!

113
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:31,680
Is it really that bad?

114
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:35,080
I think it's time to kick you in the nuts and see which is worse.

115
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:39,540
The baby's head is crowning.

116
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,920
Oh, my God!

117
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:45,340
That is the most beautiful top of a head I have ever seen.

118
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,660
- Chandler, you have to see this. - I'm okay.

119
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,900
Chandler. You don't want to miss this.

120
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,580
This is the birth of your child.

121
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:55,780
- It's the miracle of life. - All right.

122
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:01,180
Wow, that is one disgusting miracle.

123
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,600
Start pushing. Here we go.

124
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,480
Here come the shoulders.

125
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:14,920
It's a boy.

126
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,580
- Is he okay? - He's just fine.

127
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:20,260
You did it.

128
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,480
It's a baby.

129
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:24,740
A beautiful little baby.

130
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:28,040
And some other stuff I'm gonna pretend I don't see.

131
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:33,280
- Would you like to cut the umbilical cord? - Okay.

132
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:39,260
Well, that's spongy.

133
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,140
Hey, handsome.

134
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:51,520
I'll love you so much that no woman is ever gonna be good enough for you.

135
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,020
- We are so lucky. - I know.

136
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:59,340
He has your eyes.

137
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:05,000
I mean, I know that's not possible, but he does.

138
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,060
We'll just get him cleaned up a bit.

139
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:12,180
Oh, my God, he's beautiful.

140
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,760
Thank you so much.

141
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:16,940
I'm really happy for you guys.

142
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:20,180
- How do you feel? - I'm tired.

143
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,740
You don't have that much time to relax.

144
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,340
The other one will be along in a minute.

145
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:33,280
I'm sorry, who should be along in a what, now?

146
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,580
The next baby should be along in a minute.

147
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:40,140
We only ordered one.

148
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:45,140
- You know it's twins, right? - Oh, yeah.

149
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:47,660
These are the faces of two people in the know.

150
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:56,740
I can't believe you didn't know it's twins.

151
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,420
This has never happened before.

152
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:01,460
Well, gosh. That makes me feel so special and good.

153
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:04,340
Wait. Did you know it was twins?

154
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:07,120
It's here in the paperwork we got from the clinic in Ohio.

155
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,860
- Did anybody tell you? - I don't think so.

156
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:15,400
They did mention two heartbeats, but l thought it was just mine and the baby's.

157
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,660
They said, "Both heartbeats are strong."

158
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,760
And I thought, "Well, that's good, because I'm having a baby."

159
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,400
This is unbelievable.

160
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:25,320
Twins actually run in my family.

161
00:10:25,561 --> 00:10:27,101
Interesting.

162
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:29,520
Can I see you for a second?

163
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:33,840
What do we do?

164
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,420
What do you mean, "What do we do?"

165
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:35,980
Twins!

166
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:38,180
Twins!

167
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:41,000
Chandler, you're panicking.

168
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:43,040
Join me, won't you?

169
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:48,460
What do you say we keep one and then just have an option on the other one?

170
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,620
- We can't split them up. - Why not?

171
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,140
We could give each of them half a medallion.

172
00:10:54,200 --> 00:11:00,520
And then years later, they'll find each other and be reunited.

173
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,080
I mean, that's a great day for everybody.

174
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:07,220
What if the person who adopts the other one is horrible?

175
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,260
What if they're not?

176
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:10,360
What if it's adopted by a king?

177
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:12,740
Yeah. Because I hear the king is looking to adopt.

178
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:17,020
Monica, we are not ready to have two babies.

179
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:18,380
That doesn't matter.

180
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:21,020
We have waited so long for this.

181
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,640
I don't care if it's two babies.

182
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:24,100
I don't care if it's three babies.

183
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:27,720
I don't care if the entire cast of <i>Eight Is Enough</i> comes out of there.

184
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:32,220
We are taking them home because they are our children.

185
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:34,020
Okay.

186
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,400
- Okay. - Okay!

187
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:39,830
Okay.

188
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,580
It looks like we're about ready over here.

189
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:43,680
Come on, Erica.

190
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:44,840
Start pushing again now.

191
00:11:47,025 --> 00:11:51,045
- Here she comes. - She? It's a girl?

192
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:51,740
Yeah.

193
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,100
Well, now we have one of each.

194
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:58,920
And that's enough.

195
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:06,320
And then she said it was the perfect way to say goodbye.

196
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:10,320
Oh, my God. What did you say?

197
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,380
Nothing. What do you say to that?

198
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:15,120
You've got to tell her how you feel.

199
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:17,440
- No way. - Well, you can't just give up.

200
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,500
Is that what a dinosaur would do?

201
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:22,450
What?

202
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:24,020
Dude. I'm just trying to speak your language.

203
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,940
Ross, Rachel doesn't know that you even wanna get back together.

204
00:12:28,940 --> 00:12:30,780
If she did, she might feel differently.

205
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,060
She might not even go.

206
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:35,760
- You really think so? - I'm telling you!

207
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:40,420
Oh, ok, this is the part of the musical where there'd be a good, convincing song.

208
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:48,440
Hi.

209
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:50,300
Can't a girl finish a song around here?

210
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:54,580
- Hey. - Hi. I dropped Emma off at my mom's.

211
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,100
- Okay. - You're not taking her tonight?

212
00:12:56,400 --> 00:13:01,200
No. We decided I'd set up, then my mom would bring Emma to Paris on Sunday.

213
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,220
Eight-hour flight with a one year old.

214
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:03,900
Good luck, Mom.

215
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:04,740
You kidding?

216
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,860
Eight hours with my mom talking about Atkins.

217
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:07,520
Good luck, Emma.

218
00:13:10,820 --> 00:13:12,020
All right. You know what? You're right.

219
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,680
I should at least tell her how I feel.

220
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:17,020
- Ross. Wait, wait. - What? What?

221
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:18,300
Could you get me a muffin?

222
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,320
- Rachel? - Yeah?

223
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:31,000
I know you're leaving tonight, but I just have to tell you.

224
00:13:32,727 --> 00:13:34,357
I love you.

225
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:40,040
Now, I don't know if that changes your plans at all.

226
00:13:40,130 --> 00:13:44,720
But I thought you should know.

227
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,340
Gunther.

228
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,020
I love you too.

229
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:53,860
Probably not in the same way.

230
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,640
But I do.

231
00:13:56,440 --> 00:14:06,460
And when I'm in a cafe having coffee or I see a man with hair brighter than the sun I'll think of you.

232
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:14,640
- Bye, you guys. - Bye.

233
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:19,880
Oh, my God!

234
00:14:21,476 --> 00:14:23,716
Unbelievable.

235
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,200
Hey, you know what might help?

236
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,800
I'm not getting you a muffin!

237
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:39,900
Do you think they recognize each other from in there?

238
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:48,740
Maybe. Unless they're like people who've lived in apartments next to each other for years, then one day they're pushed through a vagina and they meet.

239
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,700
We're going to take Erica to Recovery now.

240
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:55,280
There's something that we wanted to tell you.

241
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:59,840
We decided to name the girl baby Erica.

242
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:03,800
Oh, my God, that's just like my name!

243
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:07,940
Son of a gun, it is.

244
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,420
Anyway, I'm gonna go get some rest.

245
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:15,780
I'm really glad I picked you guys.

246
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,580
You're gonna make great parents.

247
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,300
Even Chandler.

248
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:25,480
- Okay, well, bye. - Bye.

249
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,880
- We'll call you. - Okay.

250
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,500
Have fun at church camp.

251
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,700
- Look at these little bunnies. - I know.

252
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,600
You ready to trade?

253
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,940
- Okay. - Okay.

254
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:45,760
Okay. Let's see.

255
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,380
- We could trade later. - Yeah, I'm good.

256
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:02,780
Hey, what are you working on?

257
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:05,980
A "welcome home" sign for the baby.

258
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,700
How sweet! Oh, is that the baby?

259
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,980
No, I sat in the paint.

260
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:16,000
- Hey. - So did you talk to Rachel?

261
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:19,520
- No. And I'm not going to. - What?

262
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,240
Why not?

263
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:22,140
She's just gonna shoot me down.

264
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:23,720
You guys saw what happened with Gunther.

265
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,060
That did not look like fun.

266
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:27,260
How can you compare yourself to Gunther?

267
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:30,700
I mean, sure, he's sexy in a more obvious way.

268
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,900
You have a relationship with her.

269
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:36,420
You slept together last night.

270
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,080
Yeah, and she still wants to go.

271
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,500
It's pretty clear where she is.

272
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,980
I know what you mean. I mean, sometimes--

273
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:44,580
- Joe. - Damn it!

274
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:47,900
If I were gonna tell her,

275
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,120
I don't have to do it now.

276
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:51,360
Okay? I'll be seeing her again. We've got time.

277
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:54,340
No, you don't. She's going to Paris!

278
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:56,180
She is going to meet somebody.

279
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,660
Do you know how many hot guys there are in Paris?

280
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,680
It's a city of Gunthers.

281
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:05,620
- Hey. - Hey.

282
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:07,160
What do you have there?

283
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,660
Oh, I made a little something.

284
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:11,300
If I had more time to work on it, it'd be better, but....

285
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:15,600
Oh, my God, you did that yourself?

286
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:17,480
Honey, that's gorgeous.

287
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,600
You know, the baby can't read, Mike.

288
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:24,940
Hi. You guys. The car service just got here.

289
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,380
I can't believe they're not home yet!

290
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:28,240
I have to catch my stupid plane.

291
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:29,400
I want to see the baby.

292
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,160
Monica just called from the cab.

293
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,620
She said they should be here any minute.

294
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:35,120
Apparently, there's some big surprise.

295
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:37,060
Yeah, did she sound happy about it?

296
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:40,360
Because my friend Ethel's baby was born with a teeny-tiny beard.

297
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:46,680
- Welcome home. - Oh, my God.

298
00:17:50,490 --> 00:17:53,540
- Oh, my gosh. - Hey.

299
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,710
Hey.

300
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,320
Hey, so, what is the big surprise?

301
00:18:05,410 --> 00:18:08,000
- Oh, my God! - How did this--?

302
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,080
Okay, awkward question.

303
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:10,980
The hospital knows you took two, right?

304
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:13,460
Yes. It's twins.

305
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,220
Oh, my-- They are so cute.

306
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,080
Now, what kinds are they?

307
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,340
This is a boy. And that's a girl.

308
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,040
Her name is Erica.

309
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,280
Hey, that pregnant girl's name was Erica.

310
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:29,620
Yeah. It's a shame you two didn't get to spend more time together.

311
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,840
Yeah, and we named the boy Jack, after Dad.

312
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,240
He's gonna be so happy.

313
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:38,440
Jack Bing. I love that.

314
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,060
It sounds like a '40s newspaper guy.

315
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,660
You know, "Jack Bing, <i>Morning Gazette.</i>

316
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,920
I'm gonna blow this story wide open."

317
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,180
Oh, my gosh.

318
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:53,580
So beautiful.

319
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:54,760
I want one.

320
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,900
Oh, yeah? Well, tell me which one.

321
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:59,100
I'll try to slip it in my coat.

322
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:02,720
Seriously.

323
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:04,020
I mean, you want to make one of those?

324
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:05,600
One? How about a whole bunch?

325
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:06,740
Really?

326
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:10,900
Yeah. We can teach them to sing, and we could be like the von Trapp family.

327
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:13,260
Only without the Nazis.

328
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:14,660
Although that sounds kind of dull.

329
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,260
I can't believe this.

330
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:18,920
If I don't leave now,

331
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:19,980
I'm gonna miss my plane.

332
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,280
I'm so glad you got to see the babies.

333
00:19:22,590 --> 00:19:24,460
Me too.

334
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:28,560
I'm just sorry I'm not gonna be around to watch you two attempt to handle this.

335
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:33,840
All right. Oh, I can't say goodbye to you guys again.

336
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:37,240
- I love you all so much. - Love you.

337
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:39,340
- We love you. - Call us when you get there.

338
00:19:39,354 --> 00:19:43,254
I will. Ross, come here.

339
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:54,700
I just want you to know last night I'll never forget it.

340
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:56,980
Neither will l.

341
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:07,660
All right. Now I really have to go.

342
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,500
Okay, <i>au revoir</i>.

343
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:14,500
They're gonna really hate me over there.

344
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:19,620
So you just let her go?

345
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:21,820
Yeah.

346
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:26,780
- Hey, maybe that's for the best. - Yeah?

347
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:29,280
Yeah. You know, you just-- Look, you gotta--

348
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:32,520
You gotta think about last night the way she does.

349
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,980
Okay? You know, maybe....

350
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:39,460
Maybe sleeping together was the perfect way to say goodbye.

351
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:42,100
Now she'll never know how he feels.

352
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,920
Maybe that's okay, you know?

353
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:46,360
Maybe it is better this way.

354
00:20:47,291 --> 00:20:51,180
I mean, now.... Now you can move on.

355
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,740
I mean, you've been trying to for so long.

356
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:56,600
Maybe now that you're on different continents....

357
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:58,840
Right?

358
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,960
Maybe now you can actually do it, you know.

359
00:21:05,042 --> 00:21:09,362
You can finally get over her.

360
00:21:13,792 --> 00:21:15,622
Yeah, that's true.

361
00:21:17,196 --> 00:21:18,636
Except....

362
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:22,580
I don't want to get over her.

363
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:23,720
What?

364
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:26,000
I don't. I want to be with her.

365
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:26,680
Really?

366
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:28,200
Yeah. I'm going to go after her.

367
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,160
Yeah, you are!

368
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:33,500
Wait! Wait! Get your coat! Get your coat!

369
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:36,300
- My coat. - This is so cool!

370
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:39,020
I have no idea what's going on, but I am excited!

371
00:21:40,060 --> 00:21:41,860
What do you think she's gonna say?

372
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:42,680
I don't know.

373
00:21:43,980 --> 00:21:49,820
Even if she shoots me down, at least I won't spend my life wondering what would have happened. Where is my coat?

374
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:51,080
You didn't bring one!

375
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,160
My cab's downstairs.

376
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,240
I'll drive you to the airport.

377
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:55,580
- Wish me luck. - Hurry!

378
00:21:56,042 --> 00:21:57,362
Good luck!

379
00:22:08,417 --> 00:22:09,757
There's no seat belts!

380
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:15,320
That's okay. If we hit anything the engine will explode, so it's better if you're thrown from the car.

381
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:18,800
- All right, all right. Let's do this. - Okay!

382
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,380
- Hey! - 80th and East End.

383
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:24,100
No. I don't take passengers.

384
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,400
The law makes you accept any fare.

385
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,320
You don't understand. This cab isn't real.

386
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:30,780
What's your medallion number?

387
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:33,160
My medallion number is, get out of the cab!

388
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:35,060
- What? - Get out of the cab!

389
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:45,760
Oh, hey, can I give you guys my housewarming gift now?

390
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:47,600
- Now, that you can do. - All right.

391
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:01,800
Chick Jr.? Duck Jr.?

392
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,060
Don't hide from Mama!

393
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:16,240
You can open your eyes now.

394
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:18,480
- Are we off the bridge? - Yes!

395
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:21,060
Is the old woman on the bicycle still alive?

396
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:23,140
Yeah, she jumped right back up.

397
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,900
Oh, my God. Phoebe, slow down!

398
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:28,820
Do you want to get to Rachel in time?

399
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,960
Yes, but I don't want to die in your cab.

400
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,420
You should have thought of that before you got in!

401
00:23:35,692 --> 00:23:37,192
- Tollbooth. - What?

402
00:23:37,214 --> 00:23:39,014
Tollbooth!

403
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,900
Four bucks. There are quarters in the glove compartment.

404
00:23:44,420 --> 00:23:45,060
Hurry!

405
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:46,580
Okay.

406
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:51,920
Damn, that window's clean.

